                "text": "Read file C:\\Users\\Qbits\\Downloads\\ctx0an\\ARCHITECTURE.md, lines 1-212\n1: # CNCM Architecture Specification\n2: **Compact Causal-Hybrid Next-Concept Model**\n3: \n4: CNCM is a ground-up PyTorch architecture for **fast, memory-efficient, agent-capable text generation on edge devices** (4 GB Android smartphones, 8–16 GB consumer iGPU laptops, Apple Silicon / mobile NPUs, and desktop GPUs). It re-engineers **Next-Concept Modeling** ([HazyResearch/ncm](https://github.com/HazyResearch/ncm), Kumbong et al., *arXiv:2610.14162*) and incorporates compact edge-LLM training lessons from **MiniMind-3**, resolving vanilla NCM's codebook bloat, fixed-window non-causal context limits, and discrete VQ exact-match brittleness for Agentic AI.\n5: \n6: ---\n7: \n8: ## 1. Vanilla NCM vs. CNCM: Head-to-Head Comparison\n9: \n10: | Dimension | Vanilla `HazyResearch/ncm` | **CNCM (This Repo)** | Edge / Quality Gain |\n11: |---|---|---|---|\n12: | **Stage 1 Quantizer** | Multiscale RVQ-VAE with explicit `K × V_code × d_vq` FP32 + EMA codebook tables (`12 × 4096 × 384 = 18.87M` params, `~151 MB` w/ EMA buffers); vulnerable to collapse, DDP rank divergence, grad-accum EMA decay bug | **Multiscale Residual FSQ (`MultiscaleRFSQ`)**: zero codebook tables, zero EMA buffers; implicit $8^4 = 4096$-point scalar grid in $d_q = 4$ dims + depthwise-separable cascaded L1 convs & `DepthwiseSepPhi` + affine-free `GroupNorm` | **-18.8M params / -151 MB** eliminated; ~100% grid utilization; FP16/BF16/INT8/INT4-safe; DDP & grad-accum invariant |\n13: | **Chunk & Scale Schedule** | Fixed window $L \\in \\{128, 1024\\}$, $K = 12\\text{--}18$ levels, $\\sum \\ell_k = 641\\text{--}11{,}469$ (**5.0×–11.2×** sequence blowup); single fixed window without causal chunk chaining | Compact edge chunk $L = 64$, $K = 8$ convex schedule `(1, 2, 4, 8, 12, 20, 36, 64)`, $\\sum \\ell_k = 147$ (**2.30×** blowup) + **Causal-Prefix Block-AR** across arbitrary-length multi-turn chunks | **2.2×–4.9× lower** attention & compute blowup; unbounded multi-turn context with incremental prefix KV cache |\n14: | **Target Attention & KV Cache** | Bidirectional prefix + `block_diagonal` target scales (single-turn only; no chunk commit) | **Causal prefix** (with optional per-token INT8 KV cache + exact bottom-right causal chunk commit) + **`block_diagonal` target scales** with per-level reset 2D-safe RoPE | **0 MB target-scale KV growth**; exact train/infer parity across arbitrary multi-chunk conversations |\n15: | **Backbone Parameter Efficiency** | Standard non-looped Transformer (`8L–16L`, `768–1024d`, 88M–228M params) | **Relaxed Recursive Layer Looping (`CNCMBlock`)**: Pre-RMSNorm + QK-RMSNorm + GQA + SwiGLU; `num_unique_layers` repeated `num_loops` times with lightweight per-loop RMSNorm + low-rank residual adapters (`rank=16..32`) | **21–24 effective reasoning layers** inside `~14M–41M` unique parameters (`<15 MB` INT4 for `nano`) |\n16: | **Concept Output Head** | Flat 4096- or 8192-way softmax head (or `_TiedCodebookHead` distance lookup over large tables) | **Factorized Joint Concept Head (`FactorizedConceptHead`)**: chained autoregressive micro-head predicting $p(c_0)\\prod_{j=1}^{d_q-1} p(c_j \\mid h, c_{<j})$ over $d_q = 4$ FSQ digits | Full 4096-way joint correlation at **<0.3M params** and **>40× fewer output MACs** |\n17: | **Agentic Tool Calling & Exact Fidelity** | Pure VQ discrete decoding corrupts strict JSON, numerals (`1956→1957`), identifiers, and code markup even at 99.99% recon accuracy | **Unified Dual-Mode Backbone**: fast parallel Concept Mode for `<think>` & prose + shared **Exact-AR Mode** (`generate_exact` + `JSONSchemaConstrainedMasker`) inside `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` | **100% schema-valid JSON** tool calls even on tiny edge models; zero extra model weights |\n18: | **Decoding Acceleration & Verification** | Fixed $K$ steps always; no built-in exact verification | **Dynamic Early-Exit Confidence Gate** (`early_exit_conf`) in Concept M