{(k)} \\in \\{0,\\dots,L_j-1\\}^{B \\times \\ell_k \\times d_q}$ and continuous quantized embedding $u_q^{(k)}$.\n67: 4. Upsample back to length $L$ (`DepthwiseSepCascadeUp` initialized to nearest-repeat for $k=0$; linear/nearest interpolation for $k \\ge 1$) and refine via per-level depthwise-separable `DepthwiseSepPhi`:\n68:    $$\\Delta \\hat{z}_k = (1 - \\alpha_\\phi) \\tilde{u}_q^{(k)} + \\alpha_\\phi \\, \\text{PW}(\\text{DW}_{3\\times 1}(\\tilde{u}_q^{(k)}))$$\n69: 5. Accumulate $\\hat{z} \\leftarrow \\hat{z} + \\Delta \\hat{z}_k$ and update residual $r_{k+1} = r_k - \\Delta \\hat{z}_k$.\n70: 6. **Training Loss & Regularizers**:\n71:    $$\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{Stage 1}} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{CE}}\\big(\\text{Dec}(\\hat{z}_{\\text{drop}}),\\; x\\big) + \\beta_{\\text{commit}} \\sum_{k=0}^{K-1} \\text{MSE}\\big(z_{\\text{norm}},\\; \\text{sg}(\\hat{z}_{\\le k})\\big)$$\n72:    with **nested dropout (`fine_drop`)** truncating fine levels with probability `fine_drop_prob=0.5` so coarse prefixes $\\hat{z}_{\\le k}$ remain independently decodable (directly powering dynamic early exit at inference!).\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ### Innovation 2: Compact Edge Schedule, Causal-Prefix Block-AR & Dynamic Early Exit\n77: Vanilla NCM's $L = 128, K = 12$ ($\\sum \\ell_k = 641$, 5.0× blowup) and $L = 1024$ ($\\sum \\ell_k = 11{,}469$, 11.2× blowup) create heavy quadratic attention cost and cannot chain chunks with cached prefixes because prefix attention is bidirectional.\n78: \n79: CNCM uses an edge-optimized convex scale schedule:\n80: $$\\ell = (1, 2, 4, 8, 12, 20, 36, 64), \\qquad L = 64, \\quad K = 8, \\quad \\sum_{k=0}^{K-1} \\ell_k = 147 \\;\\; (2.30\\times L)$$\n81: \n82: **4D Attention Mask Structure (Prefix length $P$, Target concept scales $\\ell_0, \\dots, \\ell_{K-1}$):**\n83: \n84: ```text\n85:                 Prefix (0..P-1)   | L0(1)  L1(2)  L2(4)  ...  L7(64)\n86: Prefix (0..P-1) [ CAUSAL LOWER  ] | [  0     0      0    ...    0   ]\n87: ----------------+-----------------+----------------------------------\n88: Level 0 (l_0)   [ FULL PREFIX   ] | [ FULL   0      0    ...    0   ]\n89: Level 1 (l_1)   [ FULL PREFIX   ] | [  0    FULL    0    ...    0   ]\n90: Level 2 (l_2)   [ FULL PREFIX   ] | [  0     0     FULL  ...    0   ]\n91:    ...          [      ...      ] | [ ...   ...    ...   ...   ...  ]\n92: Level 7 (l_7)   [ FULL PREFIX   ] | [  0     0      0    ...   FULL ]\n93: ```\n94: \n95: - **Causal Prefix + Incremental KV Cache**: Prefix tokens attend causally with monotonic positions `[0 .. P-1]`. After a 64-token concept chunk is decoded, it is committed into the prefix KV cache in **one parallel forward pass** using an exact **bottom-right causal mask** (`k_idx <= P + q_idx`, `is_causal=False`), guaranteeing `< 1e-4` numerical equivalence to uncached full-sequence inference.\n96: - **Zero Target KV Cache Growth**: Target concept scales use **`block_diagonal`** attention with **per-level reset RoPE** (`position_ids = [0 .. l_k - 1]`). Target activations attend to the cached prefix KV and bidirectionally within their own level $\\ell_k$, and are immediately discarded before level $k+1$ (which receives the accumulated $\\hat{z}_{\\le k}$ pooled to length $\\ell_{k+1}$).\n97: - **Per-Token INT8 KV Cache (`QuantizedKV`)**: Optional symmetric per-token per-head INT8 key/value quantization halves KV-cache RAM with negligible attention drift.\n98: - **Dynamic Early-Exit Confidence Gate**: At level $k \\ge 1$, if the mean max-probability across predicted FSQ digits exceeds `early_exit_conf` (e.g., `0.92`), Concept Mode skips the remaining fine levels and decodes $\\hat{z}_{\\le k}$ directly via Stage 1's nested-dropout-trained decoder!\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: ### Innovation 3: Smarter-Per-Byte Backbone with Relaxed Recursive Layer Looping\n103: Mobile and iGPU models are strictly bounded by parameter RAM and memory bandwidth, yet multi-step reasoning benefits sharply from depth. `CNCMBlock` (`cncm/layers.py`) pairs