parallel across all $T = \\sum \\ell_k$ positions in one forward pass — enabling exact 1-pass code-space log-likelihood `compute_code_logprobs` for **GRPO / CISPO**!\n124: - **Tiny footprint**: On `nano` ($H=384, d_h=96, L_j=8$), the entire joint 4096-way head takes **~0.16M params** (vs. $384 \\times 4096 = 1.57\\text{M}$ for a single flat head, or `18.8M` for per-level untied heads) and **>40× fewer output MACs**.\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: ### Innovation 5: Unified Dual-Mode Exact-Action Agentic AI & Self-Speculative Verification\n129: Vanilla NCM's frozen VQ bottleneck introduces rare (~0.01%–1.2%) discrete token flips that catastrophically break strict JSON keys, numeric tool arguments, and code syntax. CNCM resolves this **without adding a second model**:\n130: \n131: ```mermaid\n132: stateDiagram-v2\n133:     [*] --> ConceptMode: User Prompt + Tool Schemas (Causal Prefix)\n134:     ConceptMode --> ConceptMode: Parallel Block-AR Chunks (<think>, prose)\\nK=8 steps / 64 tokens + Early Exit\n135:     ConceptMode --> ExactARMode: Emit <tool_call> (or explicit/router trigger)\n136:     ExactARMode --> ToolExec: JSONSchemaConstrainedMasker\\nGuaranteed valid {\"name\":..., \"arguments\":{...}}</tool_call>\n137:     ToolExec --> ConceptMode: Inject <tool_response>{json}</tool_response>\\ninto Causal Prefix KV Cache\n138:     ConceptMode --> [*]: Emit <|eos|> (Final Answer)\n139: ```\n140: \n141: 1. **Joint Stage 2 Training (`forward_joint`)**: Trains the shared recursive backbone simultaneously on Concept Mode (`FactorizedConceptHead` with 50% linear conditioning corruption + level-weighted loss) and Exact-AR Mode (`exact_head`, weight-tied to token embeddings) so both modes stay mutually aligned.\n142: 2. **Deterministic Grammar Constraints (`JSONSchemaConstrainedMasker`)**: During Exact-AR tool calls, a token-aware prefix automaton masks invalid next-token logits to $-\\infty$, enforcing `{\"name\": \"<registered_tool>\", \"arguments\": {<schema_validated_args>}}</tool_call>` with zero chance of malformed JSON even at 0.5M–15M parameters.\n143: 3. **Self-Speculative Decoding (`generate_self_speculative`)**: Drafts a full $L$-token chunk in $K$ parallel Concept Mode steps and verifies all $L$ tokens in **one parallel Exact-AR forward pass** against the exact same backbone, yielding mathematically **lossless greedy equivalence** to standard autoregressive decoding.\n144: \n145: ---\n146: \n147: ### Innovation 6: Plan-Guided Fill-in-the-Middle (PG-FIM) for Code & Prose Infilling\n148: Standard left-to-right concept generation cannot condition on right-side suffix context $S$, while naive PSM infilling in discrete VQ space suffers from unknown middle chunk counts, identifier drift (`total_sum` $\\to$ `total_val`), and boundary syntax collisions at the middle-to-suffix seam.\n149: \n150: PG-FIM solves all three with a 4-stage dual-mode pipeline on the same unified `CNCMModel`:\n151: \n152: ```text\n153: <fim_prefix> P <fim_suffix> S <fim_middle>  <mlen_k> <kw> kw_1 | kw_2 | kw_3 </kw>  [ Middle Concept Chunks ] <fim_end>\n154: |------------- Causal Prefix -------------|  |--- Exact-AR Plan (3-10 tokens) ---|  |-- Parallel Concept Mode (K=8) --|\n155: ```\n156: \n157: 1. **11 High-Tail PG-FIM Sentinel Tokens (`[V-11 .. V-1]`) & Edge Context Budgets**:\n158:    - `<fim_prefix>`, `<fim_suffix>`, `<fim_middle>`, `<fim_end>`, `<kw>`, `</kw>`, `<kw/>` (0-keyword escape), and length buckets `<mlen_1>`, `<mlen_2>`, `<mlen_3>`, `<mlen_4+>` (1 to 4+ chunks of 64 tokens).\n159:    - `format_fim_prompt` retains the `fim_prefix_budget=512` tokens of $P$ and `fim_suffix_budget=256` tokens of $S$ **nearest the cursor** so the causal prefix KV cache stays under 5 MB on edge devices.\n160: 2. **Exact-AR Plan Stage with `CodeSymbolTable` & `KeywordPlanMasker`**:\n161:    - `CodeSymbolTable` (`cncm/code/symbols.py`) extracts `defined_identifiers` and `used_identifiers` from $P$ and $S$ via zero-C-binary Python `ast` + lexical recovery (with opti