\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 4. Verified Engineering Pitfalls Explicitly Fixed in CNCM\n173: \n174: Every verified source-code bug discovered in `HazyResearch/ncm` and `MiniMind-3` audits is structurally prevented:\n175: \n176: 1. **2D RoPE Axis-Broadcast Bug**: `apply_rotary_pos_emb` explicitly unsqueezes `cos.unsqueeze(-2)` / `sin.unsqueeze(-2)` on `[B, S, H, D]` layout, preventing silent axis corruption when sequence length `S == num_attention_heads`.\n177: 2. **SDPA Top-Left Rectangular Causal Mask Trap**: `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` is always called with `is_causal=False` and explicit 4D additive masks; chunk commits onto cached prefixes of length $P$ use a true bottom-right causal mask (`k_idx <= P + q_idx`).\n178: 3. **`.half()` Checkpoint & Buffer Corruption**: Stage 1 M-RFSQ and integer buffers are strictly saved and executed without blind `.half()` casting (`save_checkpoint` preserves exact FP32/INT64 dtypes).\n179: 4. **EMA × Grad-Accum & DDP Codebook Divergence**: Eliminated structurally by replacing EMA VQ codebooks with stateless `MultiscaleRFSQ`.\n180: 5. **Padding Waste & Omitted Masks**: `PackedChunkDataset` slices contiguous padding-free `L=64` windows; `BlockARSFTDataset` and `train_stage2` always pass explicit `prefix_mask`.\n181: 6. **Zero-Warmup LR Instability**: All trainers use `WarmupCosineScheduler` (5–10% linear warmup + cosine decay to `0.1 * lr`).\n182: 7. **Backend Portability**: Zero CUDA-only or Triton-only kernels — runs cleanly on CPU, Windows DirectML (iGPU), Apple MPS, CUDA, and exports to ONNX opset 17+.\n183: \n184: ---\n185: \n186: ## 5. Presets & Multi-Device Edge Deployment Analysis\n187: \n188: ### Preset Specifications\n189: \n190: | Preset | Vocab $V$ | Chunk $L$ / Levels $K$ | $d_{\\text{vq}}$ / FSQ | Backbone $H$ | Unique × Loops (Eff. Depth) | Heads (Q / KV) | Target Tier |\n191: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n192: | `tiny_test` | 512 | 16 / 5 `(1..16)` | 48 / `(4,4,4,4)` | 96 | 2 × 2 (**4L**) | 4 / 2 | Fa