ase A 1-pass Exact-AR syntax/keyword span repair, optional Phase B `CopyAwareKeywordCrossAttention` Stage 1 pointer decoding, and Stage 3 Compiler-in-the-Loop GRPO (`train_pg_fim_grpo` + `run_code_sandbox`).\n12: \n13: See [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) for the complete mathematical specification, vanilla NCM comparison, and roofline analysis.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## Quickstart\n18: \n19: ```bash\n20: # 1. Install minimal pure-PyTorch core (CPU / CUDA / MPS / DirectML)\n21: pip install -r requirements.txt\n22: \n23: # 2. Run the full end-to-end demo (hardware profiles, Stage 1+2+GRPO smoke run,\n24: #    dual-mode JSON-constrained calculator agent, real INT4/INT8 quantization & ONNX wrapper check)\n25: python demo_cncm.py\n26: ```\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## Hardware-Targeted Presets\n31: \n32: | Preset | Params (S1 + S2) | Vocab | Chunk $L$ / $K$ | Effective Depth | Packed INT4 (`g=32`) | Target Hardware |\n33: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n34: | `tiny_test` | **0.38M** (`0.10M + 0.28M`) | 512 | `16` / `5` | `2 × 2 = 4L` | **0.51 MB** | Fast CPU CI & unit tests |\n35: | `nano` | **14.50M** (`1.51M + 12.99M`) | 4096 | `64` / `8` | `7 × 3 = 21L` | **12.29 MB** (`<15 MB`) | **Low-End Android** (4 GB RAM, XNNPACK/NNAPI) |\n36: | `mini` | **39.33M** (`2.56M + 36.77M`) | 4096 | `64` / `8` | `12 × 2 = 24L` | **29.67 MB** (`<30 MB`) | **Consumer iGPU Laptop** (8–16 GB RAM, DirectML/Vulkan) |\n37: | `base` | **93.04M** (`5.08M + 87.96M`) | 6400 | `64` / `8` | `12 × 2 = 24L` | **66.08 MB** | **Desktop GPU / Apple Silicon / High-End NPU** |\n38: \n39: *(Run `python demo_cncm.py --section profile` to print live hardware roofline estimates, KV-cache RAM, and HBM/LPDDR bandwidth savings.)*\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## Training Pipeline\n44: \n45: All trainers use pure PyTorch (zero CUDA-only/Triton-only dependencies), `WarmupCosineScheduler`, padding-free chunk packing, explicit `prefix_mask`, and FP32/INT64-safe atomic checkpoints:\n46: \n47: ```bash\n48: # Stage 1: Train M-RFSQ Concept Tokenizer (padding-free PackedChunkDataset + nested fine_drop)\n49: python -m cncm.trainer.train_stage1 --preset tiny_test --steps 50 --batch-size 8\n50: \n51: # Stage 2: Train Unified Dual-Mode CNCMModel (frozen Stage 1 + 50% cond corruption + Exact-AR loss)\n52: python -m cncm.trainer.train_stage2 --preset tiny_test --mode joint --steps 50 --batch-size 4\n53: \n54: # Stage 3: 1-Pass Code-Space GRPO / CISPO RL with verifiable <think>/<tool_call>/answer rewards\n55: python -m cncm.trainer.train_grpo --preset tiny_test --steps 6 --num-generations 4\n56: \n57: # Stage 3 (PG-FIM): Compiler-in-the-Loop GRPO with AST/compile/unit-test sandbox rewards\n58: python -m cncm.trainer.train_grpo --preset tiny_test --fim --steps 6 --num-generations 4\n59: ```\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## Plan-Guided Fill-in-the-Middle (PG-FIM) Usage\n64: \n65: ```python\n66: from cncm import CNCMConceptTokenizer, CNCMModel, CNCMTextTokenizer, get_preset\n67: \n68: cfg = get_preset(\"nano\", use_copy_decoder=True)\n69: tokenizer = CNCMTextTokenizer(vocab_size=cfg.vocab_size)\n70: model = CNCMModel(cfg, CNCMConceptTokenizer(cfg))\n71: \n72: res = model.generate_fim(\n73:     prefix=\"def sum_positive(items):\\n    total = 0\\n    for x in items:\\n        if x > 0:\\n\",\n74:     suffix=\"\\n    return total\\n\",\n75:     tokenizer=tokenizer,\n76:     use_plan=True,        # Emits <mlen_k> <kw> ... </kw> under KeywordPlanMasker\n77:     enable_repair=True,   # Phase A 1-pass Exact-AR syntax & keyword span repair\n78:     quantize_kv=True,     # INT8 causal prefix KV cache\n79: )\n80: print(\"Plan:\", res[\"planned_chunks\"], res[\"keywords\"])\n81: print(\"Infill:\\n\", res[\"full_text\"])\n82: ```\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## Dual-Mode Agentic AI Usage\n87: \n88: ```python\n89: from cncm import CNCMConfig, CNCMConceptTokenizer, CNCMModel, CNCMTextTokenizer, get_preset\n90: from cncm.agent import CNCMAgent, create_default_registry\n91: \n92: cfg = get_preset(\"nano\")\n93: tokenizer = CNCMTextTokenizer(vocab_size=cfg.vocab_size)\n94: model = CNCMModel(cfg, CNCMConceptTokenizer(cfg))\n95: \n96: agent = CNCMAgent(\n97:     model=model,\n98:     tokenizer=tokenizer,\n99:     registry=create_default_registry(),  # calculator, kv_memory, text_stats, clock_utc\n100:     use_grammar_constraints=True,        # 100% schema-valid JSON in Exact-AR mode\n101:     quantize_kv=True,                    # INT8 causal prefix KV cache\n102: )\n103: trace = agent.run(\"Calculate 18 * 24 + 9 using the calculator.\")\n104: print(trace.summary())\n105: ```\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: ## Edge Deployment Guide (Android & Consumer iGPU Laptops)\n110: \n111: ### 1. Real Packed INT4 / INT8 Quantization\n112: ```python\n113: from cncm.export import quantize_model_int4, measure_model_size\n114: \n115: q_model = quantize_model_int4(model, group_size=32, quantize_embeddings=True)\n116: print(measure_model_size(q_model))  # Packs 2 x 4-bit weights per uint8 + fp16 group scales/zeros\n117: ```\n118: \n119: ### 2. ONNX Graph Export (Opset 17+)\n120: ```python\n121: from cncm.export import export_cncm_onnx\n122: \n123: # Verifies all 3 pure-PyTorch edge wrappers & emits stage1_decoder.onnx,\n124: # stage2_exact_step.onnx, and stage2_concept_step.onnx when `onnx` is installed:\n125: report = export_cncm_onnx(model, out_dir=\"exports/nano_onnx\", opset=17)\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ### 3. Target Backend Setup\n129: - **Windows Consumer iGPU (Intel Iris Xe / AMD Radeon Vega)**:\n130:   Install `pip install torch-directml` (training/PyTorch inference) or `pip install onnxruntime-directml` (ONNX deployment). `cncm.trainer.train_utils.select_device(\"auto\")` detects DirectML automatically.\n131: - **Low-End Android (4 GB RAM, ARM Cortex-A55/A76)**:\n132:   Export `nano` with `export_cncm_onnx`, apply INT4 weight packing (`quantize_model_int4`), and execute via **ONNX Runtime Mobile** (XNNPACK CPU or Android NNAPI delegate) with INT8 prefix KV caching (`<15 MB` weights, `~22–30 MB` total runtime RAM).\n133: - **Apple Silicon / Desktop GPU**:\n134:   Runs natively on `mps` or `cuda` with PyTorch SDPA (`is_causal=False` explicit 4D masks).\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: ## Project Layout\n139: \n140: ```text\n141: cncm/\n142: ├── config.py              # CNCMConfig + tiny_test / nano / mini / base presets\n143: ├── text_tokenizer.py      # Lossless byte-fallback + subword tokenizer & chat/tool template\n144: ├── quantizer.py           # MultiscaleRFSQ (zero-table FSQ, DepthwiseSep L1 & Phi convs)\n145: ├── tokenizer_model.py     # Stage 1 CNCMConceptTokenizer\n146: ├── layers.py              # 2D-safe RoPE, 4D SDPA masks, Recursive CNCMBlock, INT8 KV, FactorizedConceptHead\n147: ├── model.py               # Unified Dual-Mode CNCMModel (Concept, Block-AR, Exact-AR, Self-Speculative)\n148: ├── trainer/               # PackedChunkDataset, BlockARSFTDataset, Stage 1/2 & Code-Space GRPO trainers\n149: ├── agent/                 # ToolRegistry (4 built-in tools), JSONSchemaConstrainedMasker, CNCMAgent\n150: └── export/                # Packed INT4/INT8 quantization, hardware roofline profiler, ONNX export\n151: demo_cncm.py               # Runnable end-to-end showcase CLI\n152: ARCHITECTURE.md            # Deep technical specification & vanilla NCM comparison\n153: ```\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: ## Credits & References\n158: \n159: - **Next-Concept Modeling (NCM)**: H. Kumbong et al., Stanford Hazy Research & Scaling Intelligence Lab — [*Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation*](https://github.com/HazyResearch/ncm) (arXiv:2610.14162, MIT License).\n160: - **MiniMind-3**: Compact edge-LLM architecture, small-vocabulary efficiency, and multi-stage training lessons from Jingyao Gong's MiniMind series.\n161: - **Finite Scalar Quantization (FSQ)**: Mentzer et al., *Finite Scalar Quantization: VQ-VAE Made Simple* (ICLR 2024)."
